Puerto Rico's governor's asking the  Department of Homeland Security to audit  how a small Montana power company landed  a 300 million dollar contract to help  restore electric service it was recently  revealed  Whitefish energy appears to have ties to  interior secretary ryan's inky and to  president Trump election effort Diana  Goldman is in Washington Juliana good  morning good morning Puerto Rico's  outdated power grid was especially  vulnerable ahead of the storm because  it's government power company filed for  bankruptcy in July and yet it's still  awarded a 300 million-dollar no bid  contract to a two year old company that  had only two employees at the time as  the island of Puerto Rico attempts to  pull itself out of the dark lawmakers in  both parties want to know why and how  whitefish Energy was tasked to help  rebuild power lines on the island we  don't have enough information as to the  process that went through that  Republican congressman Rob Bishop chairs  the House Committee that oversees Puerto  Rico how it was done  needs to be greater transparency and  accountability to that and that's the  goal of our committee Whitefish Energy's  largest previous federal contract was  for only 1.3 million dollars to upgrade  power lines in Arizona this appears to  be a pretty small company are they  capable of doing the job that that I  think they're being asked on Wednesday  San Juans mayor took on the company on  Twitter writing what are they afraid we  will find whitefish responded we've got  44 linemen building power lines in your  city and 40 more men just arrived do you  want us to send them back or keep  working whitefish has since apologized  for that tweet  hi I'm Andy tech Manske founder and CEO  of whitefish energy the company's ties  to the administration are under scrutiny  tech Manske knows interior secretary  ryan's inky and whitefish is based in  his hometown the energy company is  backed by HBC investments its founder  and general partner Joe Colin Etta gave  33 thousand dollars to the campaign of  then Texas governor now energy secretary  Rick Perry and : Etta and his wife gave  twenty eight thousand two hundred  dollars to support president Trump's  election the Energy Department did not  respond  to our questions the Interior Department  and whitefish say zenki played no role  in the contract and the company says :  Etta didn't either they say they got the  job in part because they were willing to  take less money up front than the other  company that was being considered nor  all right Juliana thank you
 

